This directory contains the plugin for non-interference. 
To analyze a program, follow the Sail installation guide to setup Sail.
Remember to have the newest version of Ocaml.

Running the plugin through the terminal:
1. enter wsl: 
- \sail> wsl
2. Build and install dune
- \sail> dune clean
- \sail> dune build
- \sail> dune install
3. Run the program
- \sail> sail --noninterference ./<directory>/<filename>.sail
4. To run with privilege level assumption, use the following command
- \sail> sail --noninterference ./<directory>/<filename>.sail --noninterference-security-level <privilegeLevel>

To run dead-code elimination first, please read the README file in \sail\src\sail_dead_code_elimination